  'rl.title': 'Illustrated rules', 'rl.youBottom': 'You: bottom row, your store on the right',
  'rl.common': 'In every rule set you pick one of your pits, take all its seeds and sow them one by one counter-clockwise, into your own store but never your opponent\'s. If your last seed lands in your store, you move again. When either row is empty the game ends, and whoever has more seeds in their store wins.',
  'rl.lead.kalah': 'The standard rules played around the world. A capture puts the opposite seeds and your last seed into your store.',
  'rl.lead.basic': 'Captures take only the opponent\'s seeds — one seed smaller than Kalah, for a calmer game.',
  'rl.lead.easy': 'An introduction without captures: focus on counting the sowing and on extra turns.',
  'rl.lead.sunka': 'The relay sowing of Sungka, a traditional game from the Philippines. A single move can sweep across the whole board.',
  'rl.sow.h': 'Sowing', 'rl.sow': 'Take every seed from the chosen pit and drop one into each following pit, counter-clockwise. Include your store; skip your opponent\'s. Your pits are numbered 1–6 from your left.',
  'rl.extra.h': 'Extra turn', 'rl.extra': 'If the last seed lands in your own store, you move again. It happens when a pit holds exactly as many seeds as its distance to the store (1 in pit 6, 2 in pit 5…).',
  'rl.cap.h': 'Capture (Kalah)', 'rl.cap': 'If your last seed lands in an empty pit on your side and the opposite pit has seeds, those seeds and your last seed all go to your store.',
  'rl.capB.h': 'Capture (Normal)', 'rl.capB': 'If your last seed lands in an empty pit on your side and the opposite pit has seeds, only the opponent\'s seeds go to your store; your last seed stays in the pit.',
  'rl.nocap.h': 'No captures', 'rl.nocap': 'Landing in an empty pit does nothing. The game is all about sowing and extra turns.',
  'rl.relay.h': 'Relay sowing (Sunka)', 'rl.relay': 'If your last seed lands in a pit that already holds seeds (either side), pick them all up and keep sowing. You go on until you stop in an empty pit or your store: your store gives an extra turn, an empty pit on your side captures as in Kalah, an empty pit on the other side ends your turn.',
  'rl.end.h': 'End of the game', 'rl.end': 'When all six pits of either player are empty, the game ends and the remaining seeds go to the store of the row\'s owner. In the picture the 8 seeds on top go to your opponent.',
